meta {
  name: 05 Devices After Registration
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/devices
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  `GET /devices` again.

  **Expect:** three devices now — the scanner IPC self-registered using its
  TPM identity, and the line is complete (watch its first logs arrive in the
  stream tab). Re-send until it shows up; the orchestrator registers within
  its polling interval (~a minute). If it takes longer, ask the demo operator
  to restart the orchestrator on that edge.

  A device self-registers *without* a group, so the scanner arrives with no
  `group_id` while the other two sit in `Slicing Line 2 – Cheese`. Move it
  onto the line with `PATCH /devices/{id}` (*User API → Devices*) if you want
  the fleet to read cleanly.

  The new device's `id` should match the `demoDeviceId` environment variable
  (3 for a fresh run) — the remaining steps target it.
}
